From 424e631787adad153e1d135c149eb6ab780f3037 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 26 May 2026 16:13:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0080 -- MPU-401 bit-6 DRR polling + WB
 default-flip to direct-port

WBTEST-006 H20 confirmation on g2k Vibra16S CT2490 + DreamBlaster S2
(2026-05-26): PATH=DOSMID (DOSMID-faithful direct-port MPU-401 with
bit-6 DRR polling before every byte write) produced audible piano +
bass drum where every prior path -- including the patch-0047
DSP-mediated default -- silently dropped non-note MIDI events.

Hypothesis chain in docs/internal/WBTEST-001-FINDINGS.md rev-8; the
H20 confirmation followed six in-session probe iters across this
team's wb-midi campaign. V1 polled probe stats on g2k: calls=51
iters_total=4170 iters_max=238 cap_hits=0 -> avg ~82 us per write,
max ~238 us on P54C; well within the IRQ-5 ISR service budget under
Lever 2b context.

DOSMID source provenance for the polled-write contract:
github.com/Tronix286/DOSMID, MPU401.C. The mpu401_waitwrite +
mpu401_uart functions poll bit 6 (DRR, mask 0x40) of the MPU status
register at port_base+1 and break the loop when it clears; bytes are
written only when the chip is ready to receive. The same bit-7 lie
identified by W22-WB-F MPUPROBE (TX-READY never clears on SB16 PnP
CTL0026) does NOT extend to bit 6: DRR is reliable on this hardware
and is the per-byte gate the chip expects, which the patch-0044 /
patch-0047 "BLIND write; do not poll status" comment was incorrect
to extend to ALL status bits.

The CURRENT-STATE.md "WaveBlaster status" correction 2026-05-26 is
the operator-authoritative context: WaveBlaster has NEVER actually
driven the DreamBlaster S2 wavetable in any prior release. The
patch-0047 DSP-mediated default -- which has shipped as the WB MIDI
production path since 2026-05-07 -- never produced sound through
the wavetable chip. Every prior "WB working" entry in RESULTS-MATRIX
was a misattributed silent fallback to OPL3 (the auto-detect chain
falls back when probe fails, but the W22-WB-F-era DSP-mediated path
"succeeded" at probe while still dropping all subsequent dispatch).

Patch contents:

1. Add SDL_DOSMpu401WaitDRR(port_base) static helper.
   - Polls inportb(port_base+1) & 0x40 until clear.
   - Iter cap = 10000 (~10 ms on P54C, ~40x headroom above the
     observed iters_max=238 from WBTEST-006).
   - Returns true on DRR-clear-in-time, false on cap-hit.
   - One-shot cap-warn via doskutsu_dbg_log naming the killswitch
     path (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_WB_DIRECT_PORT=0); avoids log
     spam if a chip variant has stuck-high DRR.
   - Callers fail-soft (write the byte regardless of cap-hit) so
     chips that worked unpolled still work.

2. Call SDL_DOSMpu401WaitDRR(port_base) in SDL_DOSMpu401Init_DirectPort
   before the UART entry write outportb(port_base+1, 0x3F). A
   capped-out poll at init is a strong "this chip variant does not
   honor bit 6" signal; the helper logs it once-per-process.

3. Call SDL_DOSMpu401WaitDRR(base) in the direct-port branch of
   SDL_DOSMpu401WriteByte before each outportb(base, byte). This
   is the per-byte gate that WBTEST-006 confirmed lets non-note
   MIDI events (program-change, controller, pitch-bend, etc.)
   through to the wavetable chip.

4. Flip the default of SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_WB_DIRECT_PORT from
   OFF to ON. SDL_DOSMpu401Init's dispatch now selects direct-port
   when the env var is unset (or any value other than strict "0").
   Strict-"0" killswitch reverts to the patch-0047 DSP-mediated
   path (kept as opt-in fallback). The dispatch comment block,
   init banner text, and shutdown reset value all updated to
   match the new default. The static s_mpu401_use_dsp default
   value is also flipped to false to match.

5. Init banner text updated from "mpu401: blind init at port_base="
   to "mpu401: direct-port init at port_base=" so the runtime
   witness reflects that the write is no longer truly "blind"
   (bit-6 polling now gates every write).

Cost on real-HW: ~82 us avg / ~238 us max per direct-port write per
WBTEST-006 probe. With music tempo on Cave Story MIDI ~5-10
events/sec sustained + bursts up to ~50 events/sec at scene boundaries,
the per-flip wall-clock impact is well below the 1 ms floor and
inside the IRQ-5 ISR service budget. Cap-hits=0 in the reference
probe so the worst-case ~10 ms cap is purely a defensive bound.

DOSBox-X smoke gate: doskutsu.exe + AUDIO_BACKEND=wb boots, hits
title screen, no crash. DOSBox-X has no DreamBlaster S2 daughterboard
so no audible MIDI -- the smoke gate is the WB backend init log line
emit, the chip-state-doesn't-hang condition, and absence of crash.
The cap-hit log may appear under DOSBox-X if its emulated MPU-401
keeps bit 6 stuck high; that's expected and fine -- the fail-soft
write happens regardless.

Workspace-local; never upstreamed per [[sdl_ai_policy]] -- this
patch and the broader doskutsu vendor/SDL/ tree carry doskutsu-
specific behavior changes that have no place in libsdl-org/SDL
master. The vendor/SDL/CLAUDE.md AI restriction scopes to PR
contributions; this patch series stays local to patches/SDL/.

Docs update in companion: docs/internal/BOOT.md
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_WB_DIRECT_PORT entry updated to document
the new default-ON + strict-"0" killswitch semantics.

See:
  - docs/internal/WBTEST-001-FINDINGS.md rev-8 (H20 confirmation chain)
  - docs/internal/CURRENT-STATE.md "WaveBlaster status" correction
  - github.com/Tronix286/DOSMID MPU401.C (DRR poll provenance)
  - patches/SDL/0047 (DSP-mediated path; now opt-in fallback)
  - patches/SDL/0044 (direct-port blind-init body)
