-       showed that direct-port MPU-401 access causes lockups under SDL load
-       on real SB16 PnP CTL0026. The DSP-mediated path (DSP cmd 0x34 enter
-       UART + cmd 0x38 dispatch) was probe-validated on the same hardware
-       in section 10. DSP-mediated funnels all chip access through one
-       bus contender (port 0x22C), eliminating cross-firmware races.
-
-       Direct-port path (Option A from analysis) retained behind opt-in
-       hint SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_WB_DIRECT_PORT=1 for hardware where
-       DSP-mediated turns out to be fragile. Strict-1 env-var match per
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0080): default = direct-port +
+       bit-6 DRR polling.
+
+       WBTEST-006 H20 confirmation on g2k Vibra16S CT2490 + DreamBlaster
+       S2: PATH=DOSMID (DOSMID-faithful direct-port with bit-6 DRR
+       polling before every write) produced audible piano + bass drum
+       where every prior path -- including the patch-0047 DSP-mediated
+       default -- silently dropped non-note MIDI events. Probe stats
+       (V1 polled): calls=51 iters_total=4170 iters_max=238 cap_hits=0
+       -> avg ~82 us per write, max ~238 us on P54C; well within IRQ-5
+       ISR budget under Lever 2b. See docs/internal/WBTEST-001-FINDINGS.md
+       rev-8 for the hypothesis chain.
+
+       The patch-0047 DSP-mediated path stays in-tree as an opt-in
